A||N||5||FieroSTETZ||overheating...||||5
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||09-12-1999||09:41 PM||||my '86 SE 2M6 has, for the last three to four days had a little overheating problem. i went to the market (about 10 minutes away) bought some bread, and then, on the way home at a light, steam came out of my front hood area, then it peed coolant EVERYWHERE. my car was idling at 2000 RPM. I unplugged the battery, and then re-connected it, and get error code 15: "Coolant temperature sensor or curcuit fault - signal voltage high" what the heck is this? AND, how can I get my idle down to a more reasonable level? one more! what is that screw on top of the throttle, and is the Holley throttle stock? someone help me out, this is my only transportation, and i have to get to school tomorrow. how do i fix the overheating?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-12-1999||10:15 PM||||Check the fan belts......<P>then pull out the thermostat and refill the system and let it run a bit. If it stops the thermostat went south. replace the thermostat or it won't run right. You can run it enough to test, but don't drive it like that.<P>don't forget to clear the codes from the ECM. likely it's a false code.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-12-1999).]||||reg||9
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-13-1999||02:50 AM||||Check for a cracked EGR tube, the high idle and overheat problem are typical with a real bad vacuum leak.<P>Mike||||reg||4
Z||000003||mshill||09-13-1999||04:50 AM||||MY radiator popped a leak last week.  It spilled it's guts right in the middle of the Smog Test.<P>I would check hoses and radiator for leaks.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||09-13-1999||07:13 PM||||I installed a new thermostat and cleared all the error codes prior to my post... the new error code was/ is still 15... and theres no leak on my radiator, the coolant actually BOILED out. anyone know what the coolant temperature sensor is/ where it is/ how to fix?||||reg||4
Z||000005||Dale||09-14-1999||02:32 AM||||The CTS is located on the passenger side of the motor,  pretty close to the MAP sensor(little black box 3"X 1.5" mounted on the intake manifold) The CTS can also have an affect on your Idle.  Definatly replace it (cheap)then check to see if your radiator fan is coming on when warm.||||reg||6
